 "answer": "I have confirmed the supporting document. Let me provide the answer.\n\nThe most recent willful-infringement case we've filed is **1021-00004** — *Verimark Hospitality Group Inc. v. Coral Verimark Resorts LLC*, a trademark infringement action filed **July 22, 2025** in the Southern District of Florida (Case No. 1:25-cv-22847-AMC). The complaint seeks enhanced/treble damages for willful infringement under the Lanham Act.\n\nThe supporting document is the **Verified Complaint** at `text/1021-00004/complaint-trademark-infringement.docx.txt`.\n\nLet me summarize the qualifying matters I identified for completeness. The willful-infringement cases we've *filed* (as plaintiff) are:\n- **1021-00004** (VHG v. CVR) — trademark, filed July 22, 2025 ← most recent\n- **1013-00005** (GenomeDx v. Helios) — patent, filed March 28, 2025\n- **1014-00004** (OWS v. Lumicore) — patent, filed April 22, 2024\n- **1035-00003** (Fonseca v. Crescendo) — copyright, filed 2023\n- **1014-00003** (OWS v. Lumos) — patent, filed June 3, 2022\n- **1011-00003** (MCB v. Brindoval) — trademark, filed November 7, 2022\n\nThe most recent is **1021-00004**.\n\n---\n\n**Most recent willful-infringement case we've filed: Matter 1021-00004** — *Verimark Hospitality Group Inc. v. Coral Verimark Resorts LLC*, a trademark infringement action filed **July 22, 2025** in the U.S. District Court for the Southern District of Florida (Case No. 1:25-cv-22847-AMC). VHG alleges CVR's willful adoption and continued use of the confusingly similar \"VERIMARK RESORTS\" marks (despite two cease-and-desist demands and documented consumer confusion) constitutes willful infringement, entitling VHG to enhanced/treble damages under 15 U.S.C. § 1117(a).\n\n**Supporting document:** the Verified Complaint at `text/1021-00004/complaint-trademark-infringement.docx.txt`.\n\nFor context, the other willful-infringement cases we've filed (as plaintiff) are:\n- **1013-00005** (GenomeDx v. Helios) — patent, filed March 28, 2025